      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Electrical stimulation in the lateral midbrain reticular formation (LRF) inhibited the responses of spinal dorsal horn neurons to noxious (50 degrees C) skin heating. Systemic administration of naloxone (0.1-2 mg/kg) had no effect on inhibition produced by LRF stimulation in 10 units, while this inhibition was partially blocked in 3 units. The results indicate that endogenous opiates are not primarily involved in mediating descending inhibition from LRF stimulation."},
